            <ArticleTitle>Accessory ossicles and sesamoid bones: recognition and treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7748/en.22.10.27.e1404</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Accessory ossicles and sesamoid bones are normal variants of bone development. In foot and ankle X-rays these bones can appear similar to, or can obscure, fractures, which makes the X-rays difficult to interpret. This article illustrates and describes some of the more common ossicles and sesamoid bones, and provides a brief description of the management of the patients with foot or ankle pain whose X-rays are inconclusive.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
